Synchronize hook removal with PipeWire event-loop dispatch. Keep the native
Qt 6.10.2 ABI and system style plugins; do not replace the audio backend.

The first change is the upstream lifetime backport above. The second is an
AutoTalk correction: report unsuccessful portal responses through the existing
capture error interface after resetting request state. The final changes keep
registry callbacks scoped to the portal-selected source and stop their event
loop before stream teardown. They do not repair KDE.

--- a/src/multimedia/pipewire/qpipewire_async_support.cpp
+++ b/src/multimedia/pipewire/qpipewire_async_support.cpp
@@ -84,3 +84,5 @@ CoreEventListener::~CoreEventListener()
 {
-    removeHooks();
+    QAudioContextManager::withEventLoopLock([&] {
+        removeHooks();
+    });
 }

